WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[Music]

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.000
The My Shipments page gives you a centralized view of all your inbound shipments to Amazon.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.000
From this page, you can track shipment status.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Search for specific shipments.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
And take action without navigating away from your queue.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:27.000
To get started, sign in to your seller account and navigate to the Manage Shipments page.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.000
You will find it within the Manage drop-down menu.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:37.000
The page displays your shipments in a table format, showing details like shipment name, status,

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:42.000
created date, and last updated date.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:47.000
If you sell in multiple marketplaces, you will also see a marketplace indicator next to each shipment.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:54.111
This flag shows which marketplace the shipment is associated with, so you can avoid mixing shipments

00:00:54.111 --> 00:00:55.000
across regions.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:59.000
To narrow your view, use the filter options at the top of the table.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:05.750
You can filter shipments by status, such as ready to ship, or shipped, to focus on the shipments

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:08.000
that need your attention right now.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:13.478
For example, if you want to see only shipments that are missing a tracking number, apply that filter

00:01:13.478 --> 00:01:15.000
to surface just those items.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:21.632
This helps you build a shipment you need to take action on, view instead of scanning your entire

00:01:21.632 --> 00:01:22.000
queue.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.000
If you are looking for a specific shipment, use the search function.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:34.000
You can search by shipment ID, status, missing tracking number, or last updated date.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:41.000
You can also use suggested timeframes to find shipments that may be stalled or need follow-up.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:45.000
Use shipment ID search when you are troubleshooting a specific order.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:51.000
Use the last updated timeframe filter to identify shipments that have not moved recently.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:56.000
To review the details of a shipment, select view next to the shipment.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.000
This opens a side panel with a summary of that shipment.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:07.000
The side panel shows the shipment name, shipment ID, created date, and unit count.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:12.667
It also displays a status progression tracker, so you can confirm where your shipment is in the

00:02:12.667 --> 00:02:13.000
process.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:20.000
In transit, delivered, received, or closed.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:27.000
Within the shipment list, you can see a quick summary of the units and SKUs included in each shipment.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:31.000
Use this to validate quantities before drilling into the details.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:37.000
If something looks incorrect, you can address it early before it becomes a larger inventory issue.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:42.464
To adjust how the table displays, use the table customization options which can be found via the

00:02:42.464 --> 00:02:46.000
gear icon on the top right of the screen called preferences.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:54.000
You can change which columns appear, reorder them, and set how many rows show per page.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:03:00.222
Start by selecting the columns most relevant to your daily workflow such as status, last updated,

00:03:00.222 --> 00:03:01.000
and tracking.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:07.000
Move those to the front, and hide columns you do not use.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:14.000
This reduces noise and speeds up your review, especially if you manage a high volume of shipments.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:19.000
Once you have configured your filters and columns, you can save that setup as a named view.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:24.542
Select the option to save your current view and give it a name that reflects its purpose, such as

00:03:24.542 --> 00:03:26.000
needs tracking or in transit.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:31.400
The next time you visit my shipments, you can load that saved view instead of rebuilding your filters

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:32.000
from scratch.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:38.632
This is especially useful if you check the same set of shipments regularly as part of your daily

00:03:38.632 --> 00:03:39.000
operations.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:46.000
From my shipments, you can access the send to Amazon workflow by selecting a shipment or order ID.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:51.000
You can continue your inbound workflow from there as you normally would.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:55.000
You can also access capacity manager from this page.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:01.000
Use it as you do today to monitor your capacity limits and plan inbound shipments.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:08.000
The My Shipments page brings your inbound shipment management into one place, with tools to filter.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:16.000
Search, customize, and save your view for faster daily operations.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:21.846
Start by setting up a saved view that matches your most common workflow and use the side panel to

00:04:21.846 --> 00:04:24.000
check shipment progress without leaving your queue.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:30.667
To learn more about managing your inbound shipments, visit Seller University for additional resources

00:04:30.667 --> 00:04:34.000
on send to Amazon and inventory management.
 (

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:40.011
upbeat music)
